# 15. Largest BST in Binary Tree

**a2z-350**

Given an arbitrary Binary Tree, find the size of the largest subtree that is itself a BST. 

Example:

```text
        5
       / \
      2   4
     / \
    1   3
```

The whole tree isn't a BST because:

```text
4 < 5
```

But:

```text
      2
     / \
    1   3
```

is a BST.

Answer:

```text
3
```

The expected solution is a postorder traversal carrying BST validity, size, minimum and maximum values. ([GeeksforGeeks][1])

---

## Approach 1 — Check every subtree

For every node:

1. Check whether its subtree is a BST.
2. If yes, calculate its size.
3. Otherwise check left and right.

### Complexity

```text
Worst case: O(N²)
Space: O(H)
```

Good as a first approach, but not the interview-optimal solution.

---

## Approach 2 — Postorder DP

For each node return:

```text
isBST
size
min
max
```

A node forms a BST if:

```text
left.isBST
AND
right.isBST
AND
left.max < node.val
AND
node.val < right.min
```

Then:

```text
size = left.size + right.size + 1
```

### Java

```java
class TreeNode {
    int val;
    TreeNode left;
    TreeNode right;

    TreeNode(int val) {
        this.val = val;
    }
}

class Info {
    boolean isBST;
    int size;
    int min;
    int max;

    Info(boolean isBST, int size, int min, int max) {
        this.isBST = isBST;
        this.size = size;
        this.min = min;
        this.max = max;
    }
}

public class Solution {

    public static int largestBST(TreeNode root) {
        return solve(root).size;
    }

    private static Info solve(TreeNode root) {

        if (root == null) {
            return new Info(
                true,
                0,
                Integer.MAX_VALUE,
                Integer.MIN_VALUE
            );
        }

        Info left = solve(root.left);
        Info right = solve(root.right);

        if (left.isBST &&
            right.isBST &&
            left.max < root.val &&
            root.val < right.min) {

            return new Info(
                true,
                left.size + right.size + 1,
                Math.min(root.val, left.min),
                Math.max(root.val, right.max)
            );
        }

        return new Info(
            false,
            Math.max(left.size, right.size),
            Integer.MIN_VALUE,
            Integer.MAX_VALUE
        );
    }
}
```

