# 14. Correct BST With Two Nodes Swapped

**a2z-349**

Two nodes of an otherwise valid BST are accidentally swapped. Restore the BST.

Example:

```text
Original:

      3
     / \
    1   4
       /
      2
```

`2` and `3` are misplaced.

---

## Approach 1 — Inorder + sort

BST inorder traversal should be sorted.

Store:

```text
inorder values
```

Find the two values that violate sorted order.

Then swap them.

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(N)
Space: O(N)
```

Easy to explain.

---

## Approach 2 — O(H) extra space using inorder

We don't actually need to store the complete inorder traversal.

Maintain:

```text
prev
first
middle
last
```

Whenever:

```text
prev.val > current.val
```

we found an inversion.

For the first inversion:

```text
first = prev
middle = current
```

For a second inversion:

```text
last = current
```

Then:

```text
if last != null
    swap(first, last)
else
    swap(first, middle)
```

### Java

```java
class Solution {

    TreeNode first = null;
    TreeNode middle = null;
    TreeNode last = null;
    TreeNode prev = null;

    public void recoverTree(TreeNode root) {

        inorder(root);

        if (first != null && last != null) {
            int temp = first.val;
            first.val = last.val;
            last.val = temp;
        }
        else if (first != null && middle != null) {
            int temp = first.val;
            first.val = middle.val;
            middle.val = temp;
        }
    }

    private void inorder(TreeNode root) {

        if (root == null)
            return;

        inorder(root.left);

        if (prev != null && prev.val > root.val) {

            if (first == null) {
                first = prev;
                middle = root;
            }
            else {
                last = root;
            }
        }

        prev = root;

        inorder(root.right);
    }
}
```

### C#

```csharp
public class Solution
{
    private TreeNode first;
    private TreeNode middle;
    private TreeNode last;
    private TreeNode prev;

    public void RecoverTree(TreeNode root)
    {
        Inorder(root);

        if (first != null && last != null)
        {
            Swap(first, last);
        }
        else if (first != null && middle != null)
        {
            Swap(first, middle);
        }
    }

    private void Inorder(TreeNode root)
    {
        if (root == null)
            return;

        Inorder(root.Left);

        if (prev != null && prev.Val > root.Val)
        {
            if (first == null)
            {
                first = prev;
                middle = root;
            }
            else
            {
                last = root;
            }
        }

        prev = root;

        Inorder(root.Right);
    }

    private void Swap(TreeNode a, TreeNode b)
    {
        int temp = a.Val;
        a.Val = b.Val;
        b.Val = temp;
    }
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time:  O(N)
Space: O(H)
```

If recursion is counted, `H` is stack space.

