# 10. Construct BST from Preorder

**a2z-345**

Example:

```text
preorder = [8, 5, 1, 7, 10, 12]
```

Construct:

```text
        8
       / \
      5   10
     / \    \
    1   7    12
```

---

## Approach 1 — Insert each value

Start with empty BST.

Insert values one by one.

### Complexity

Average:

```text
O(N log N)
```

Worst case:

```text
O(N²)
```

---

## Approach 2 — Bounds

This is optimal.

Preorder tells us:

```text
root → left subtree → right subtree
```

Maintain an upper bound.

For example:

```text
preorder = 8,5,1,7,10
```

At node `8`:

```text
left values < 8
right values > 8
```

### Java

```java
private static int index = 0;

public static TreeNode bstFromPreorder(
        int[] preorder) {

    index = 0;

    return build(
        preorder,
        Integer.MAX_VALUE
    );
}

private static TreeNode build(
        int[] preorder,
        int upperBound) {

    if (index == preorder.length ||
        preorder[index] > upperBound) {

        return null;
    }

    int value = preorder[index++];

    TreeNode root = new TreeNode(value);

    root.left = build(preorder, value);

    root.right = build(preorder, upperBound);

    return root;
}
```

### C#

```csharp
