# 9. LCA in BST

**a2z-344**

Given:

```text
        6
       / \
      2   8
     / \ / \
    0  4 7  9
```

LCA of:

```text
2, 8
```

is:

```text
6
```

---

## BST property gives O(H)

At node:

```text
if p < root && q < root
    go left

if p > root && q > root
    go right

otherwise
    root is LCA
```

### Java

```java
public static TreeNode lca(
        TreeNode root,
        int p,
        int q) {

    while (root != null) {

        if (p < root.val && q < root.val) {
            root = root.left;
        }
        else if (p > root.val && q > root.val) {
            root = root.right;
        }
        else {
            return root;
        }
    }

    return null;
}
```

