# 8. Validate BST

**a2z-343**

Check whether a binary tree is a valid BST. 

---

## Approach 1 — Inorder

A valid BST has strictly increasing inorder traversal.

```text
1 2 3 4 5
```

If we ever get:

```text
previous >= current
```

it's invalid.

### Java

```java
public static boolean isValidBST(TreeNode root) {

    Stack<TreeNode> stack = new Stack<>();

    TreeNode current = root;

    long previous = Long.MIN_VALUE;

    while (current != null || !stack.isEmpty()) {

        while (current != null) {
            stack.push(current);
            current = current.left;
        }

        current = stack.pop();

        if (current.val <= previous)
            return false;

        previous = current.val;

        current = current.right;
    }

    return true;
}
```

### C#

```csharp
public static bool IsValidBST(TreeNode root)
{
    Stack<TreeNode> stack = new Stack<TreeNode>();

    TreeNode current = root;

    long previous = long.MinValue;

    while (current != null || stack.Count > 0)
    {
        while (current != null)
        {
            stack.Push(current);
            current = current.Left;
        }

        current = stack.Pop();

        if (current.Val <= previous)
            return false;

        previous = current.Val;

        current = current.Right;
    }

    return true;
}
```

---

## Approach 2 — Range validation

Every node gets a valid range.

```text
root:
(-∞, +∞)

left:
(-∞, root)

right:
(root, +∞)
```

### Java

```java
public static boolean isValidBST(TreeNode root) {
    return validate(
        root,
        Long.MIN_VALUE,
        Long.MAX_VALUE
    );
}

private static boolean validate(
        TreeNode root,
        long min,
        long max) {

    if (root == null)
        return true;

    if (root.val <= min ||
        root.val >= max)
        return false;

    return validate(
            root.left,
            min,
            root.val)
        &&
        validate(
            root.right,
            root.val,
            max);
}
```

### C#

```csharp
public static bool IsValidBST(TreeNode root)
{
    return Validate(
        root,
        long.MinValue,
        long.MaxValue
    );
}

private static bool Validate(
    TreeNode root,
    long min,
    long max)
{
    if (root == null)
        return true;

    if (root.Val <= min ||
        root.Val >= max)
        return false;

    return Validate(root.Left, min, root.Val)
        && Validate(root.Right, root.Val, max);
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(N)
Space: O(H)
```

**Important trap:** don't use `Integer.MIN_VALUE` / `Integer.MAX_VALUE` as bounds if node values themselves can equal those values. Use `long`/`long.MinValue` and `long.MaxValue`.

