# 6. Delete a Node in BST

**a2z-341**

Three cases.

### Case 1 — Leaf

```text
    5

delete 5

    null
```

### Case 2 — One child

Replace node with its child.

### Case 3 — Two children

Replace value with:

```text
inorder successor
```

which is the minimum node in the right subtree.

Then delete that successor.

---

## Java

```java
public static TreeNode deleteNode(
        TreeNode root,
        int key) {

    if (root == null)
        return null;

    if (key < root.val) {

        root.left =
            deleteNode(root.left, key);

    }
    else if (key > root.val) {

        root.right =
            deleteNode(root.right, key);

    }
    else {

        // No left child
        if (root.left == null)
            return root.right;

        // No right child
        if (root.right == null)
            return root.left;

        // Two children
        TreeNode successor =
            findMin(root.right);

        root.val = successor.val;

        root.right =
            deleteNode(
                root.right,
                successor.val
            );
    }

    return root;
}

private static TreeNode findMin(TreeNode root) {

    while (root.left != null)
        root = root.left;

    return root;
}
```

### C#

```csharp
public static TreeNode DeleteNode(
    TreeNode root,
    int key)
{
    if (root == null)
        return null;

    if (key < root.Val)
    {
        root.Left = DeleteNode(root.Left, key);
    }
    else if (key > root.Val)
    {
        root.Right = DeleteNode(root.Right, key);
    }
    else
    {
        if (root.Left == null)
            return root.Right;

        if (root.Right == null)
            return root.Left;

        TreeNode successor =
            FindMin(root.Right);

        root.Val = successor.Val;

        root.Right =
            DeleteNode(
                root.Right,
                successor.Val);
    }

    return root;
}

private static TreeNode FindMin(TreeNode root)
{
    while (root.Left != null)
        root = root.Left;

    return root;
}
```

Complexity:

```text
Time: O(H)
Space: O(H) recursive
```

Iterative implementation can achieve:

```text
Space: O(1)
```

