# 4. Floor in BST

**a2z-339**

Floor of `X`:

> Largest value `<= X`.

Example:

```text
BST values = [2, 4, 6, 8, 10]

X = 7

floor = 6
```

---

## Java

```java
public static int floor(
        TreeNode root,
        int x) {

    int answer = -1;

    while (root != null) {

        if (root.val == x)
            return root.val;

        if (root.val < x) {

            answer = root.val;
            root = root.right;

        } else {

            root = root.left;
        }
    }

    return answer;
}
```

