# BST Interview Cheat Sheet

This is the part I'd memorize for interviews:

| Problem            | Core idea                 |   Time | Extra space |
| ------------------ | ------------------------- | -----: | ----------: |
| Search             | Compare and go left/right |   O(H) |        O(1) |
| Min/Max            | Extreme left/right        |   O(H) |        O(1) |
| Floor/Ceil         | Track candidate           |   O(H) |        O(1) |
| Insert             | Compare and descend       |   O(H) |        O(1) |
| Delete             | 0/1/2 child cases         |   O(H) |       O(H)* |
| Kth smallest       | Inorder                   | O(H+K) |        O(H) |
| Validate BST       | Range / inorder           |   O(N) |        O(H) |
| LCA                | BST direction property    |   O(H) |        O(1) |
| Construct preorder | Bounds                    |   O(N) |        O(H) |
| Successor          | Candidate + go left       |   O(H) |        O(1) |
| Merge BSTs         | Two inorder iterators     | O(N+M) |    O(H1+H2) |
| Two Sum            | HashSet / 2 iterators     |   O(N) | O(N) / O(H) |
| Recover BST        | Inorder inversions        |   O(N) |        O(H) |
| Largest BST        | Postorder information DP  |   O(N) |        O(H) |

* Recursive deletion uses call-stack space; iterative deletion can be `O(1)`.

